; The ONE variable: `layout_direction = 3` on a TOP icon-mode ItemList. TOP
; mode takes a DIFFERENT pair of RTL branches from LEFT mode: the icon mirror
; centres the icon in its row first (item_list.cpp:1553) and the label
; keeps HORIZONTAL_ALIGNMENT_CENTER while its whole box is mirrored
; (:1639-1641), where LEFT mode instead re-derives the pen and swaps to
; RIGHT. Both lists are the same width and hold the same two rows, and each
; row is far narrower than the list, so a box that failed to mirror would sit
; at the opposite edge. unit-item-list-rtl.tscn covers the LEFT-mode pair and
; unit-item-list.tscn is TOP mode at the default direction, so a regression in
; the TOP-mode mirror is invisible in both.

